# Cloudflare Pages reads a file literally named `_headers` from your build
# output root and applies these rules automatically - no dashboard config
# needed. Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# These two headers make the page cross-origin isolated, which is what
# unlocks SharedArrayBuffer - required for PSP's only available EmulatorJS
# core build (ppsspp-thread-wasm.data). See README "Cross-origin isolation".
#
# credentialless, NOT require-corp: this project loads EmulatorJS's
# loader.js and its core/data files from cdn.emulatorjs.org (or your own
# self-hosted /data/ folder). COEP: require-corp requires every
# cross-origin resource on the page to send back its own
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy header opting in - cdn.emulatorjs.org does
# not send this, which was confirmed live in production (ROM Player by
# Coops, the app this wrapper's tuning is ported from): require-corp
# silently killed every fetch to the CDN (net::ERR_FAILED with no HTTP
# status - looks like an outage, isn't one), breaking EVERY core's boot,
# not just PSP's. credentialless still yields crossOriginIsolated===true
# (all PSP needs) without requiring third-party CORP cooperation - use it
# unless you've independently confirmed your specific CDN mirror sends
# CORP headers.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
